:: D03_FallAsleep [nobr]
<div class="prose-block">

<p>Sleep comes faster tonight. The body is tired from three orgasms this afternoon and the kind of emotional exhaustion that leaves you hollowed out but clean, like a house after a storm blew through and took everything that wasn't nailed down.</p>

<p>I dream in fragments. A hallway of mirrors, long and narrow, lit from above by fluorescent tubes that flicker and buzz. Every reflection is female but wearing something different, different clothes, different hair, a different expression each time. One wears a cocktail dress and heels. One wears scrubs and sneakers. One wears nothing at all and stands with a confidence I don't recognize in myself. One wears Marcus's grey hoodie over women's jeans, looking scared, looking small, looking exactly like I do right now.</p>

<p>I reach for that one. She reaches back. Our fingertips touch the glass at the same time.</p>

<p>She smiles.</p>

<p>I wake up hours later and don't remember any of it right away. My face is wet, though. I think I was crying in my sleep.</p>

